<p>Kanye West, also known as Ye, postponed a concert planned for Marseille, France, after French authorities weighed blocking the performance. The move came days after the UK denied him entry over repeated antisemitic remarks and statements praising Adolf Hitler. The Marseille show had been scheduled for June, and the delay adds to growing restrictions on West’s live appearances in Europe. Pressure around the event had been building after Marseille’s mayor publicly opposed the concert. His stance highlighted how local officials and national governments are weighing anti-hate concerns and public-order questions when high-profile performances are planned.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/58vg-m0pJCPjPCloD5K_c9c6Kypom_zsAFaeC8EXPH1Df378IpVZokgB94PeUvyr9B5AvCqirezAJ3t5Rxq-8vTnMFLfhu1wvpJ3HOOgHnDA1PuAun0mi3PaPTrSHyqF2lYe_HCOSM7wuMSDMNlO8gVyxGlHkXaV3_xLg2ZbHx8' alt='Ye announced that he had postponed a concert in Marseille, France.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Timing: West announced the postponement Tuesday night, about a week after the UK government said it would block him from entering the country.</li><li>French process: Reports say French authorities were weighing whether to stop the show, but they do not say a final formal ban was issued before West postponed it.</li><li>Different mechanisms: In the UK, the immediate result was the loss of a Wireless Festival headline slot. In France, the immediate question was whether the planned June date in Marseille could go ahead.</li></ul><blockquote>A showcase for those who promote hatred - Benoît Payan</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Marseille Mayor Benoît Payan: He said the city should not host the concert because he did not want Marseille to become a platform for people who promote hatred. (<a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/04/15/world/europe/kanye-west-ye-france-concert.html'>The New York Times</a>)</li><li>UK government: British authorities denied West entry to the country earlier in April, a decision that cost him his Wireless Festival slot. (<a href='https://www.dw.com/en/kanye-west-postpones-france-concert-after-uk-visa-denial/a-76785732'>Deutsche Welle</a>)</li><li>French authorities: Officials were considering whether to block the Marseille performance, signaling that France was reviewing whether the event should go ahead at all. (<a href='https://www.lemonde.fr/en/france/article/2026/04/15/kanye-west-postpones-marseille-concert-after-france-considers-blocking-him-from-performing_6752436_7.html'>Le Monde</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.youtube.com/shorts/jpanzeX9ilk'>Kanye West Marseille concert postponed after anti-Semitic remarks • FRANCE 24 English</a> - youtube.com</li><li><a href='https://www.lemonde.fr/en/france/article/2026/04/15/kanye-west-postpones-marseille-concert-after-france-considers-blocking-him-from-performing_6752436_7.html'>Kanye West postpones Marseille concert after France considers blocking him from performing</a> - lemonde.fr</li><li><a href='https://www.dw.com/en/kanye-west-postpones-france-concert-after-uk-visa-denial/a-76785732'>Kanye West postpones France concert after UK visa denial</a> - dw.com</li><li><a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/c36rrrp5wnlo'>Kanye West postpones France gig following UK ban</a> - bbc.com</li><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/04/15/world/europe/kanye-west-ye-france-concert.html'>Kanye West Postpones Concert in France as Government Considers Banning It</a> - nytimes.com</li></ul>